        "timestamp": 1779350679,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Israeli minister Ben-Gvir's video of Gaza flotilla activists sparks outcry Middle East Issued on: 21/05/2026 - 10:04 Detained activists, their hands tied and forced to kneel as the Israeli national anthem is belted out in the background. Israeli National Security Minister Itamar Ben-Gvir released footage on X of him taunting the activists from a Gaza-bound flotilla. The video sparked widespread international condemnations. FRANCE 24’s Gabrielle Nadler reports. Iran ‘prefers diplomacy’ but if there’s a war, Tehran says it’s ready 20/05/2026 Middle East 'Huge mismatch' between Iran, US and Gulf States' expectations, analyst says 19/05/2026 Middle East US, Iran trade threats as Tehran stages mass weddings for couples ready for 'sacrifice' 19/05/2026 Middle East Trump says holding off on strike on Iran at request of Gulf allies 19/05/2026 Middle East Stalled US-Iran talks show \"Trump's strategy of pressure\" is not paying off 19/05/2026 Middle East Iran officially announces new body to manage Strait of Hormuz 18/05/2026 Middle East Iran sets up new Strait of Hormuz managing body amid stalled talks with US 18/05/2026 Middle East G7 finance ministers meet amid Middle East war economic fallout 18/05/2026 Middle East Israeli attacks in Gaza have stepped up since halt in bombing in Iran 18/05/2026 Middle East"
